# Enforce LF line endings for all text files, on every platform.
#
# Without this, line-ending behaviour depends on each contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting. Assets in this repo are regenerated by running the
# `specify` CLI, which on Windows can emit CRLF files. A CRLF blob committed
# that way still looks like a clean "new file" in `git diff --stat`, but it
# breaks shell scripts on the Ubuntu CI runner and makes the next Ubuntu
# regeneration rewrite the file to LF, producing a phantom whole-file diff in
# the daily auto-update PR.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary; detected binary files are left
# untouched. `eol=lf` stores text blobs as LF and checks them out as LF
# everywhere, so regenerations are stable across operating systems.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Be explicit for the shell scripts that run on the Linux CI runner: CRLF in a
# script produces `bad interpreter` / `\r` command-not-found failures.
*.sh text eol=lf
